Quran Reciter Voiceprint License
Version 1.0, 25 October 2026

This license covers the voiceprint gallery in this repository
(catalog.json, embeddings.safetensors, embeddings.bin) and the
identification code shipped next to it (reciter_identifier.py,
handler.py). It does not cover the TitaNet encoder. That file is
not in this repository. Its weights stay under the NVIDIA NeMo
license (CC-BY-4.0) and the sherpa-onnx ONNX package that
redistributes them.

You may use, copy, and share this gallery and this code for
closed-set identification of the enrolled Quran reciters, including
inside an application, if you do all of the following:

1. Give credit. Name this gallery, and name NVIDIA TitaNet-Small
   as the encoder. A link to the Hugging Face model page is enough.
2. Keep this license with every copy of the gallery.
3. Do not sell the gallery on its own. Using it inside a free or
   paid Quran application is allowed. Selling the vectors, or a
   model that is only these vectors, is not.
4. Do not use the gallery, the scores, or the encoder to clone,
   imitate, or impersonate a reciter, and do not present a
   synthetic voice as one of these reciters.
5. Do not use it to identify private people, or any speaker who is
   not one of the enrolled public recitations.
6. State clearly when a clip is below the published threshold and
   is therefore unknown. Do not force a name onto a weak score.

The numbers were computed from short clips of recordings indexed by
the mp3quran.net API. This repository does not contain that audio.
Rights in the recordings stay with their reciters and publishers.
If you rebuild the gallery, follow the source site's terms and
keep the same enrollment rules, or the vectors will not match this
release.

THE GALLERY AND THE CODE ARE PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF
ANY KIND. IDENTIFICATION CAN BE WRONG. A SCORE IS NOT PROOF OF WHO
IS SPEAKING.
